# Tests for the Ptc_net module (Form 8962 lines 26 to 29, Table 5)

Run with `clerk test`. The concrete cases of issue #34, worked out by hand from
Table 5 of the Instructions for Form 8962 (2024) (`sources/forms-instructions/i8962--2024.pdf`
p 17): excess APTC $2,000 repays $375 / $950 / $1,575 (Single) or $750 / $1,900 /
$3,150 (other) below 200 / 300 / 400 percent, and all $2,000 at 400 and above.

> Using Types
> Using Ptc_net as N

## Helper: excess APTC of $2,000 (line 24 = $3,000, line 25 = $5,000)

```catala
declaration scope Excess2000:
  context filing_status content Types.FilingStatus
  context percent content decimal
  n scope N.NetPtc
  output repay content money

scope Excess2000:
  definition n.filing_status equals filing_status
  definition n.household_income_as_percent equals percent
  definition n.tax_family_size_is_zero equals false
  definition n.total_ptc_amount_allowed equals $3,000
  definition n.total_aptc_amount_taken equals $5,000
  definition repay equals n.excess_aptc_repayment
```

## Single

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestSingleBands:
  a scope Excess2000
  b scope Excess2000
  c scope Excess2000
  d scope Excess2000
  e scope Excess2000

scope TestSingleBands:
  definition a.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition a.percent equals 190.0
  definition b.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition b.percent equals 250.0
  definition c.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition c.percent equals 350.0
  definition d.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition d.percent equals 400.0
  definition e.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition e.percent equals 401.0
  assertion a.repay = $375
  assertion b.repay = $950
  assertion c.repay = $1,575
  assertion d.repay = $2,000
  assertion e.repay = $2,000
  # known-bad outputs are rejected: the unlimited amount, the other-status amounts
  assertion a.repay != $2,000
  assertion a.repay != $750
  assertion b.repay != $1,900
  assertion c.repay != $3,150
```

## Other filing statuses

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestOtherBands:
  mfj scope Excess2000
  mfs scope Excess2000
  hoh scope Excess2000
  qss scope Excess2000
  mfj3 scope Excess2000
  hoh4 scope Excess2000

scope TestOtherBands:
  definition mfj.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition mfj.percent equals 190.0
  definition mfs.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingSeparately
  definition mfs.percent equals 250.0
  definition hoh.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.HeadOfHousehold
  definition hoh.percent equals 350.0
  definition qss.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.QualifyingSurvivingSpouse
  definition qss.percent equals 100.0
  definition mfj3.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition mfj3.percent equals 350.0
  definition hoh4.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.HeadOfHousehold
  definition hoh4.percent equals 400.0
  assertion mfj.repay = $750
  assertion mfs.repay = $1,900
  assertion hoh.repay = $2,000
  assertion qss.repay = $750
  assertion mfj3.repay = $2,000
  assertion hoh4.repay = $2,000
```

Head of household at 350 percent: the other column is $3,150, so the whole
$2,000 is repaid (the lesser of line 27 and line 28).

## Edges of the bands and small excess

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestBandEdges:
  at200 scope N.NetPtc
  at300 scope N.NetPtc
  at399 scope N.NetPtc
  small scope N.NetPtc

scope TestBandEdges:
  definition at200.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition at200.household_income_as_percent equals 200.0
  definition at200.tax_family_size_is_zero equals false
  definition at200.total_ptc_amount_allowed equals $0
  definition at200.total_aptc_amount_taken equals $5,000
  definition at300.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition at300.household_income_as_percent equals 300.0
  definition at300.tax_family_size_is_zero equals false
  definition at300.total_ptc_amount_allowed equals $0
  definition at300.total_aptc_amount_taken equals $5,000
  definition at399.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition at399.household_income_as_percent equals 399.0
  definition at399.tax_family_size_is_zero equals false
  definition at399.total_ptc_amount_allowed equals $0
  definition at399.total_aptc_amount_taken equals $5,000
  definition small.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition small.household_income_as_percent equals 150.0
  definition small.tax_family_size_is_zero equals false
  definition small.total_ptc_amount_allowed equals $100
  definition small.total_aptc_amount_taken equals $300
  assertion at200.line28 = $950
  assertion at200.excess_aptc_repayment = $950
  assertion at300.line28 = $1,575
  assertion at399.line28 = $1,575
  # excess below the limit: repay the excess
  assertion small.line27 = $200
  assertion small.excess_aptc_repayment = $200
  assertion small.net_ptc_credit = $0
```

## Net PTC positive: line 31, no repayment

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestNetPositive:
  n scope N.NetPtc

scope TestNetPositive:
  definition n.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition n.household_income_as_percent equals 190.0
  definition n.tax_family_size_is_zero equals false
  definition n.total_ptc_amount_allowed equals $4,800
  definition n.total_aptc_amount_taken equals $1,800
  assertion n.net_ptc_amount = $3,000
  assertion n.line26 = $3,000
  assertion n.net_ptc_credit = $3,000
  assertion n.line27 = $0
  assertion n.excess_aptc_repayment = $0
  assertion n.net_ptc_credit != $0
  assertion n.excess_aptc_repayment != $3,000
```

## Net PTC zero

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestNetZero:
  n scope N.NetPtc

scope TestNetZero:
  definition n.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition n.household_income_as_percent equals 250.0
  definition n.tax_family_size_is_zero equals false
  definition n.total_ptc_amount_allowed equals $2,000
  definition n.total_aptc_amount_taken equals $2,000
  assertion n.net_ptc_credit = $0
  assertion n.excess_aptc_repayment = $0
```

## Tax family size zero (DF workaround): repay everything

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestFamilySizeZero:
  n scope N.NetPtc

scope TestFamilySizeZero:
  definition n.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition n.household_income_as_percent equals 0.0
  definition n.tax_family_size_is_zero equals true
  definition n.total_ptc_amount_allowed equals $0
  definition n.total_aptc_amount_taken equals $2,000
  assertion n.line28 = $0
  assertion n.excess_aptc_repayment = $2,000
```
